## So What?

The dominant pattern from today: the front-of-site framing still claims something different from what the back-of-site honest assessment documents. Badge mismatches, label inversions, unexplained status changes — nearly every P0 fix is honesty-propagation, not new content. The framework has done the honest self-assessment work; it's not being surfaced to first-time readers.

The genuinely new research direction finding: the γ definitional collision (γ=2 universal vs γ=2/√Ncorr operational) is the foundational ambiguity generating multiple downstream problems. Until it's resolved with a single coherent definition and derivation, the framework can't cleanly answer "why Ncorr=1 for galaxy rotation fits?" — which is the load-bearing question behind the MOND-shared results. The explorer's γ-related topic queue (ncorr-operational-definition-recipe.md, ncorr-scale-invariant-definition.md) is directly connected.
